       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg. At that dose the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema.\n\nPlease check whether one of these was intended:\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily**, the usual starting dose. 2.5 mg is used for frail patients or those with hepatic impairment.\n- **3 mg or another dose**, if the 30 was a typo.\n\nIf you really do want 30 mg, tell me and give me the clinical reason. I can enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
